    "problem": "HostAssetPinV1.assetManifestPath must lie under assetRoot, and the completeness law requires that no unlisted regular file exists under assetRoot. The manifest is itself a regular file there. If it must list itself, its own sha256 and bytes become self-referential and unsatisfiable; if it is simply omitted, the completeness law refuses every valid bundle.",
    "resolution": "Exclude precisely one path, and only that path, from the member inventory: the manifest named by the pin. The manifest is covered by its own independent pin, so excluding it loses no coverage.",
    "exactRules": [
      "assetManifestPath lies under assetRoot and names a regular file.",
      "assetManifestPath must NOT appear as an asset row. A row whose path equals it refuses MANIFEST_SELF_LISTED, so the self-referential digest can never arise.",
      "Completeness reads: every regular file under assetRoot, EXCEPT exactly the one path assetManifestPath, must appear as an asset row; any other unlisted regular file refuses EXTRA_UNLISTED_FILE.",
      "The exclusion is by exact path equality with the pinned value, never by prefix, suffix, filename pattern or directory. Only one file is ever excluded.",
      "Coverage is therefore total: every byte under assetRoot is covered either by an asset row's digest or by HostAssetPinV1.assetManifestSha256."
    ],
